  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 102 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe intense upper trough is digging and ejecting into the OK/TX\nPanhandle. The trough will become more negatively tilted this evening\nwith intense dynamic lift expected to overspread the area after 21z.\nThe surface low should drop toward the KS/OK this evening with \nsevere storms likely to develop across southern Kansas then forming \ninto a line and racing northeast toward at least some part of the \nCWA. Damaging winds with perhaps a squall line mesovortex risk may \ndevelop across the southeast half of the CWA mainly from 4pm through \n11pm. Heavy rains will also occur given record PWATs of over 1.5\" \nagain today. Expect areas of 1-2\" with some swaths of 3-4\" tonight \ninto early Tuesday. The severe risk should end by midnight exiting to\nthe east. Additional showers and isolated storms will persist in the\nvicinity of the upper low through Tues morning with another half \ninch of rain likely on the backside of the upper system before ending\nby late in the day.\n\nAnother weaker system will shear across the region Weds into Thu\nhowever any precip should be light and limited to the southern half\nof the area. The weather looks dry after that through the weekend.",
